<h1>optimal polyphase merge</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="polyphmerge.html"><em>polyphase merge</em></a> which seeks to minimize the number of merge passes by allocating output runs of each pass to the various output files.  Since polyphase merging must have a different number of runs in each file to be efficient, one seeks the optimal way of selecting how many runs go into each output file.  A series of <a href="kthOrderFibonacci.html"><em>kth order Fibonacci numbers</em></a> is one way to select the number of runs.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="merge.html"><em>merge</em></a>, <a href="polyphmerge.html"><em>polyphase merge</em></a>, <a href="optimalMerge.html"><em>optimal merge</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorASK">ASK</a></p>

